{{define "notesIntro"}}- String literals consisting of a single word should begin with a dot (`.`).
- Complex boolean filters can be composed using `and`, `or`, and `not`.
- You can group conditions using parentheses `(` and `)`.
  **Note on Shell Escaping:** Since the shell treats parentheses specially, you must escape or quote them when invoking the CLI, e.g., `\( c.age gt .10 or c.age lt .20 \)` or `"\(" c.age gt .10 or c.age lt .20 "\)"`.
- Valid comparison operators are: `eq`, `contains`, `icontains`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`.{{end}}
